+# Seattle itinerary — October 22–25, 2026
+
+## Constraint summary
+
+- **Travelers and dates:** Maya and Leo, Thursday, October 22 through Sunday, October 25, 2026.
+- **Rail:** Arrive at King Street Station at 09:40 Thursday; depart King Street Station at 18:40 Sunday.
+- **Lodging:** Pine Street Guesthouse for all three nights, with the traveler's stated bag hold before check-in and after checkout.
+- **Mobility:** No car. Use public transit and walking, with estimated walking held to 4.0 miles or less per day.
+- **Pace:** Exactly two anchor activities per day; evenings after 20:00 remain unscheduled.
+- **Interests and food:** Public art, independent bookstores, gardens, local history, and one vegetarian meal idea daily.
+- **Corrected fixed commitment:** The remote call is at the hotel on Saturday, 10:00–12:00 PT. Friday 13:00–15:00 is available and assigned to Elliott Bay Book Company; the former Friday call is not retained.
+- **Friday/Saturday balance:** Each day has one primarily indoor anchor and one primarily outdoor anchor. Friday uses an outdoor-focused route through Pike Place Market's mixed covered/outdoor area; each day also has an indoor rain fallback.
+- **Sunday boundary:** Sightseeing ends at 14:00. After that, the plan uses only the guesthouse, the transfer to King Street Station, and the station.
+
